---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { BUY_URL, PRICE, LICENSES_EMAIL, DOWNLOAD_URL } from "../lib/product.mjs";
---

<Layout
  title="Download DiskPrune — notarized for macOS"
  description="Download DiskPrune. Notarized and Developer ID signed for macOS 14+. Double-click to open — no security warnings."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-prose px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Download DiskPrune</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Notarized, Developer ID signed, and stapled. macOS opens it with a
      double-click — no Gatekeeper warning, no "Open Anyway" step.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={DOWNLOAD_URL}>Download DiskPrune.dmg</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={BUY_URL}>Buy lifetime — {PRICE}</a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-subtle">macOS 14 Sonoma or later · Universal (Apple Silicon + Intel)</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Installing DiskPrune</h2>
    <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-muted">
      <li>Open <strong class="text-ink">DiskPrune.dmg</strong> — a window appears with the app icon.</li>
      <li>Drag <strong class="text-ink">DiskPrune.app</strong> into the <strong class="text-ink">Applications</strong> folder shortcut.</li>
      <li>Eject the disk image (drag it to the Trash, or press <kbd class="font-mono text-sm">⌘E</kbd>).</li>
      <li>Open Finder → Applications → double-click <strong class="text-ink">DiskPrune</strong>.</li>
      <li>First launch: macOS asks if you're sure. Click <strong class="text-ink">Open</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-subtle">
      That's it. No right-click tricks, no System Settings detour. The app is notarized.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Full Disk Access (optional)</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      DiskPrune scans without Full Disk Access, but some protected folders
      (Mail, Messages, Time Machine) only show byte counts — not filenames — unless
      you grant it. Grant it in System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Full Disk Access.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Already bought?</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Your license key is in the email from <strong class="text-ink">{LICENSES_EMAIL}</strong>.
      Paste it in DiskPrune → Settings → Licence. Cleanup requires a verified key;
      scanning is always free.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={DOWNLOAD_URL}>Download DiskPrune.dmg</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/support">Support</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
